    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is code-generated from this spec at build time via openapi-generator).\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added:\n- `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"java(telephoneDisplay(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`.\n- A `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default method that splits off the country code (1 digit for the `+1`/`+7` plans, 2 otherwise) and groups the national digits in threes separated by spaces \u2014 e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. It returns the raw value unchanged for non-E.164 strings and `null` when absent.\n\nThe consuming code path (controller \u2192 `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`) required no changes since the mapper already produces the DTO returned by the endpoint.\n\n**Tests:** The target test `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` (asserting `$.telephone` = `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
